    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d614">

                <pb facs="0460" n="456" sameAs="frus:frus1938v04/pg456"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">393.1163AM33/95: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Japan</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Grew</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tokyo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1938-08-26T20:00:00+09:00">August 26, 1938—8
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received August 26—9:16 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>560. Department’s 297, August 25, 4 p.m.,<anchor n="73" xml:id="d614-f1"/>
                    bombing of Southern Baptist Mission at Pingtu. In conference today with the Vice
                    Minister for Foreign Affairs I drew his attention to our note No. 975 of June
                        28,<anchor n="74" xml:id="d614-f2"/> which has not been answered and asked
                    for an early reply. Horinouchi promised immediate investigation.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Grew</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
